course: dictionary
lesson: 5912
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. The sentence around it tells you which meaning is right. «On Saturday we went to the market and bought apples from a stall.» Here a market is a place with stalls where people buy and sell.
explain: Now read this: «The market for old bikes is small, so few people want to buy them.» Market does not mean a place here. The clue is want to buy: it means how many people want to buy something.
explain: Always check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. Try "a place with stalls" in «the market for old bikes». It does not make sense, so the meaning must be about buyers.
fact: A market is a place, often outdoors with stalls, where people buy and sell food and other things.
fact: «Market» can also mean how many people want to buy something.
fact: The stock market is where people buy and sell parts of companies.
fact: «On the market» means for sale.
fact: «Market» can be a verb: to market something means to tell people about it so they buy it.
exercise: «At a night market in Thailand a child your age buys a paper cone of fried crickets.» What is a market here? | A school for children | A kind of cricket game | A paper cone | *A place with stalls where people buy and sell
exercise: «The market for old bikes is small, so few people want to buy them.» What does market mean here? | *How many people want to buy something | A place with stalls | A type of bike | A company's secret plan
exercise: «Clothes given to clothes banks are sorted: good ones are resold, many are shipped abroad to markets.» Find and copy one word that means sold again. | clothes | sorted | rags | *resold
test: «The stock market is where people buy and sell parts of companies.» What does the stock market sell? | Food and clothes | Stalls and tables | *Parts of companies | Paper cones of fried crickets
test: Mia says, «I will market my cakes at the school fair.» What does market mean here? | *Tell people about her cakes so they will buy them | A place to buy things | Build a stall at the fair | Count how many people want cakes
exam: «Their capital, Tenochtitlan, had causeways, canals, floating gardens and a huge market.» In this sentence, what would people do at the market? | *Buy and sell food and goods | Sail to Europe | Build causeways | Count the canals
